# DbAccounts — project knowledge

Cross-platform **PostgreSQL role maintenance** desktop app: manage clusters, batch-run role operations via **user-defined PostgreSQL functions** (not direct DDL in app).

## Product decisions (do not regress)

| Topic | Decision |
|-------|----------|
| UI shell | **Wails v2** + embedded WebView; frontend is vanilla HTML/CSS/JS in `frontend/` |
| DB driver | **pgx/v5**; direct **TCP** to `host:port` (no SSH tunnels in v1) |
| Secrets | Optional per-cluster `connect_user` + `password` (both editable in the cluster editor; password is a masked field with a reveal toggle, stored plain-text in the private config written mode `0600`). Auth: user = cluster `connect_user` → `PGUSER` → **OS login user** (like psql); password = cluster `password` → `PGPASSWORD` → `~/.pgpass` → **empty** (trust, like psql). Production gated by a confirm popup (no checkbox). |
| Role logic | App calls **call templates** with `${placeholder}` → `SELECT fn($1,...)` — real DDL/privileges live in **DB functions** on each cluster |
| Categories | = cluster groups. Editable in Settings (label + base `color` + `confirm` flag); id is a slug of the label. Colours applied via a generated `<style id="cat-colors">` keyed on `data-cat` (no hardcoded prod/uat colours). `confirm` drives the production popup. |
| DB function specs | User will provide real names/signatures; defaults in `config.example.yaml` are placeholders (`your_schema.*`) |

